 # Changelog
 
-## v0.1.1-r1 — 2026-10-06
-
-- Hotfix only: robust canonical/marker-based E010/E011 discovery.
-- `run_all.cmd` now requires `PREPARED_FULL` and stops before a partial control campaign can be mistaken for the full factorial tournament.
-- Added `run_controls.cmd` for intentionally running only diagnostic analytic controls.
-- UPSTREAM_PLAN records resolved E010/E011 paths relative to the Workbench root.
-- No scientific thresholds, factor levels, polarity gates, or physics operators changed.
-
-## v0.1.1 — 2026-10-06
-
-- Full-factorial skeleton × binary twist-knot × polarity design.
-- Prospective two-normalization polarity gate.
-- Complete 5_2/6_1 assignment cube and provider-stratum envelope.
-- Mutual-energy separation response diagnostics.
-- Constant-final-time spatial dynamics convergence and extended temporal refinement.
-- Independent C++/NumPy backend qualification.
-- Stronger blind seal and semantics.
-
-## v0.1.0
-
-- Initial blind nucleon topology architecture tournament.
+## v0.2.0
+- Adds re-blinded dynamical certification after v0.1.1 reveal.
+- Adds preregistered BASIC/EXTENDED/FULL linked mixed-composition cohorts.
+- Adds centroid-separation restoring probes and a diagnostic regularized mutual-energy Hessian.
+- Adds breathing, curvature-windowed torsion-sensitive and Kelvin-like transverse mode families.
+- Adds multi-epsilon projected Jacobian and spatial `N` convergence.
+- Adds nonlinear least-stable-mode ringdown.
+- Adds nontrivial RPO search and a conditionally gated nonlinear relative time-T return map projected to a preregistered physical subspace.
+- Preserves the rule: no accepted RPO, no true Floquet interpretation.
+- Adds provider-envelope reveal contrasts without a weighted winner score.
+- Adds cross-platform Gilbert provenance fallback: exact raw source + record id + frozen E010 loader-manifest; non-Gilbert geometry hashes remain byte-exact.
+- Removes tangential marker velocity from nonlinear certification dynamics as gauge.
+- Makes relative-equilibrium residual diagnostic-only to prevent post-hoc thresholding from v0.1.1.
+- Adds explicit Kelvin-restricted spectrum alongside the full coupled-mode spectrum.
