+# Scientific scope — A054 v0.1.1
+
+## Primary question
+
+Does a reproducible `2+1` circulation-polarity preference survive after collective skeleton and local twist-knot identity are independently factorized?
+
+The design is:
+
+```text
+skeleton       = U, G, B
+component 1    = 5_2 or 6_1
+component 2    = 5_2 or 6_1
+component 3    = 5_2 or 6_1
+polarity       = +++, -++, +-+, ++-
+normalization  = per-component or fixed-total
+provider       = full E011 5_2 x 6_1 anchor envelope
+```
+
+The complete binary component cube is essential: it separates the effect of a local `5_2 -> 6_1` substitution from composition-level and skeleton-level changes.
+
+## Primary reveal contrasts
+
+Reveal computes matched `G-U`, `B-U`, and `B-G` contrasts at fixed binary assignment and provider stratum, all 12 directed single-site edges of the three-bit cube, and the interaction between reversed-circulation slot and revealed knot identity.
+
+## Not in scope
+
+No mass, charge, atomic, gravity, or absolute-energy target enters this release. No proton or neutron identity is assigned by the blind evaluator. Historical `5_2^2 6_1` / `5_2 6_1^2` interpretation is reveal-only context.
+
+The finite-difference separation-energy response is diagnostic. Full constrained energy Hessians and Kelvin/Floquet certification remain downstream.
